Nothing retrieved from the corpus ever reaches a prompt - not triage's, not the agent's - and a guard asserts it by refusing to let either module import `services/rag.py`. This is a capability deliberately given up: an agent that knew how a problem was fixed last time would be better at its job. The reason is reach. The corpus is built from tickets whose payloads were written by whoever can put a line on a consumed topic, and indexing turns a document that steers one investigation into one that can be retrieved for every future ticket resembling it, invisibly. A panel keeps a person between the corpus and any decision.

An embedding is readable by whoever may read **its ticket**, not merely by whoever holds `view_ticketembedding`. A document is a verbatim copy of its ticket, so every route to one is a route to ticket text: the REST viewset, the UI viewset and the filterset each narrow the corpus to tickets the reader may view, and there is deliberately no GraphQL type, because Nautobot restricts a GraphQL type on that type's own model permission with no hook for a parent-object restriction. For the same reason `document` is not a free-text search predicate - a filter answers by narrowing, and so would report which closed tickets contain a given string without ever returning the field that matched.
